# width: 120
# `ui.dock.mode = .always` with `ui.dock.placement = .outer`: the other
# placement, where the strip takes the SCREEN's last row rather than the
# editor area's. `launcher_dock_always.test` is the shipped default
# (`.inner`, the strip above the statusline); this file keeps the row
# arithmetic of the outer one, which nothing else pins.
#
# At 120x40 that row is 39, under the `:` line — which moves to 38, and
# the statusline to 37. The click below is the proof: if the strip were
# anywhere else it would land on the `:` row instead.
#
# The run is centred (`ui.dock.align`, `.center` out of the box) and the
# `+` ends it (dock-polish). // changed (railmove): the four first-party
# surfaces are on it, so at 120 the row is ` Browser  Claude Code  Codex
# HTTP  New terminal  + New ` from column 25: New terminal at 68..83,
# column 78 its word (`launcher_dock_always.test` has the full
# arithmetic).
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
ex dock outer
expect screen contains "dock: below the command line"
ex dock always
expect screen contains "dock: always"
expect screen contains "󰐕 New "
expect screen contains "Browser"
expect screen contains "New terminal"
expect screen contains "󰐃"
# The `:` line is row 38 now, and the strip's own row 39 opens nothing.
click 110 38
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":true"
key esc
click 100 39
expect status contains "\"cmdline\":false"
# A click on New terminal opens a shell…
click 78 39
wait 900
expect pane Terminal
# …and the shell joins the strip as a running item, told from the rest
# by brightness — no dot (`launcher_dock_always.test` checks the mark).
expect screen lacks "•"
